---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_237",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 237,
  "text": "[[926.23]] <b>195₁.  Erster Ansatz ERSTER ANSATZ </p>\n<p> [[926.24]] <p><k>Generalia</k>. Substantia, qualitas, quantitas, mutatio, relatio, locus, tempus. </p>\n<p> [[926.25]] <k>Specialia</k>. <b>Sensus <tab/>externi</b>: tactus, gustus, odor, sonus, visus </p>\n<p> [[926.26]] <tab/><b>interni</b>: potentia agendi, voluntas, ratio, memoria. </p>\n<p> [[926.27]] Substantiarum seu rerum discrimina, et relationes seu praedicata primitiva et\n[[926.28]] resultantia. </p>\n<p> [[927.1]] Substantiarum discrimina possunt intelligi <b>qualitates</b>; possunt percipi <b>quantitates</b>. </p>\n<p> [[927.3]] Individualia seu haecceitates ubi <b>locus</b> et <b>tempus</b>.\n[[927.4]] <petit> </p>\n<p> [[927.5]] <i>Die folgenden drei, in Kleindruck wiedergegebenen Tabellen hat Leibniz gestrichen und durch die vierte\n[[927.6]] ersetzt</i>:\n [[927.7]] ^&.bb <Leibniz special character>Praedicatum <tab/>est^&.b</i> <Leibniz special character> <tab/><picture>502</picture> <tab/>primarium ut albedo,\n [[927.8]] Praedicatum <tab/>est\n [[927.9]] <tab/>resultans ut similitudo cum alio albo, relatio\n[[927.10]] <tab/><picture>502</picture> <tab/>status\n [[927.11]] <tab/>est\n [[927.12]] <tab/>mutatio\n[[927.13]] <tab/><picture>502</picture> <tab/>distinctum seu manifestum\n [[927.14]] <tab/>est\n [[927.15]] <tab/>confusum seu occultum\n[[927.16]] <tab/><picture>502</picture> <tab/>conceptibile, qualitas\n [[927.17]] <tab/>est\n [[927.18]] <tab/>perceptibile, quantitas </p>\n<p> [[927.19]] ^&.bb <Leibniz special character>Praedicatum est <tab/>perceptibile^&.b</i> <Leibniz special character> <tab/><picture>502</picture> <tab/>positio\n [[927.20]] <tab/><picture>502</picture> <tab/>perceptibile\n [[927.21]] Praedicatum<tab/>est <tab/>quantitas\n [[927.22]] <tab/>conceptibile </p>\n<p> [[927.23]] ^&.bb <Leibniz special character>Praedicatum est <tab/>primarium <tab/>pe<tab/>rceptibile <tab/><b>quantitas</b> <tab/>seu manifestum <tab/>status^&.b</b> <Leibniz special character> </p>\n<p> [[927.24]] <tab/><picture>502</picture> <tab/>locus <tab/><picture>407</picture> <tab/><picture>507</picture> <tab/>status\n [[927.25]] <tab/><picture>502</picture> <tab/><b>positio</b>\n [[927.26]] <tab/><picture>506</picture> <tab/>perceptibile <tab/>tempus\n [[927.27]] <tab/><b>quantitas</b> </p>\n<p> [[927.28]] <tab/><picture>506</picture> <tab/>primarium\n [[927.29]] <tab/><picture>502</picture> <tab/>confusum seu occultum\n [[927.30]] <tab/>conceptibile\n [[927.31]] Praedicatum est <tab/>distinctum seu manifestum\n [[927.32]] <tab/>(<b>qualitas</b> <tab/>mutatio\n [[927.33]] <tab/>seu forma, species)\n [[927.34]] <tab/>resultans: <b>relatio</b> </petit>\n [[928.1]] ^&.bb <Leibniz special character>praedicata necessaria sui subjecti <tab/>Nomen^&.b</i> <Leibniz special character>\n [[928.2]] <b>Nomen <Fn><i>Zu dieser Tabelle</b>: Sic optime</Fn> substantivum est</b> <tab/><b>Nomen substantivum singulare est</b>\n [[928.3]] quod omnia continet <tab/>quod omnia continet\n [[928.4]] praedicata necessaria <tab/>praedicata etiam accidentalia seu contingentia\n [[928.5]] sui subjecti<tab/>sui subjecti\n[[928.6]] ^&.bb <Leibniz special character>Pra<tab/>edicatum seu <tab/>primarium <tab/>mutatio <tab/>perceptibilis <tab/>quantitas <tab/>locus^&.b</i> <Leibniz special character> </p>\n<p> [[928.7]] <tab/><picture>305</picture> <tab/><k>manifesta</k> seu </p>\n<p> [[928.8]] <tab/>intelligibilis 1) </p>\n<p> [[928.9]] <tab/><picture>306</picture> <tab/>conceptibilis </p>\n<p> [[928.10]] <tab/> <k>qualitas</k> <tab/><k>occulta</k> seu </p>\n<p> [[928.11]] <tab/><picture>308</picture> <tab/>status <tab/>sensibilis 2) </p>\n<p> [[928.12]] <tab/><picture>303</picture> <tab/><k>quantitas</k> 3) </p>\n<p> [[928.13]] <tab/><picture>307</picture> <tab/>primarium <tab/>perceptibilis <tab/><picture>303</picture> <tab/><k>locus</k> 4) </p>\n<p> [[928.14]] <tab/><k>positio</k>\n [[928.15]] Praedicatum seu <tab/><k>tempus</k> 5)\n [[928.16]] <tab/>Nomen <tab/>mutatio\n [[928.17]] <tab/>adjectivum <tab/>id est <k>actio - passio</k> 6) </p>\n<p> [[928.18]] <tab/>resultans, <k>relatio</k> 7) </p>\n<p> [[928.19]] Hic enumero praedicata simplicia quae ex pluribus diversis non componuntur in\n[[928.20]] recto. </p>\n<p> [[928.21]] Etiam apud Geometras res differunt: <b>positione</b>, <b>magnitudine</b>, <b>specie</b> seu\n[[928.22]] qualitate. </p>\n<p> [[928.23]] Relatione res non differunt per se, sed ob differentias primarias. </p>\n<p> [[928.24]] Neque in relationibus fit mutatio, nisi quia primaria praedicata mutantur. Unde\n[[928.25]] philosophi quoque Peripatetici ajunt, motum seu mutationem non terminari ad relationes. </p>\n",
  "number": "195₁.",
  "title": "Erster Ansatz",
  "date": null
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:195₁. Erster Ansatz ERSTER ANSATZ Generalia. Substantia, qualitas, quantitas, mutatio, relatio, locus, tempus. Specialia. Sensus externi: tactus, gustus, odor, sonus, visus interni: potentia agendi, voluntas, ratio, memoria. Substantiarum seu rerum discrimina, et relationes seu praedicata primitiva ...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>